          },
          "description": "<p><span style=\"color: #800000;\"><strong>Available for Pre-Order!</strong></span><span> Contact your <a href=\"https://amaco.com/find-a-distributor/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AMACO distributor</a> to place your pre-order for the Pearlescent Glaze Series. Get your order in early to be among the first to receive these new glazes when they become available.</span></p>\n<p>P-65 Sienna Frost is a fluid, orange-tan with iridescent mottling where thick.</p>\n<p><strong>Food Safe:</strong> Tested for lead and cadmium release in accordance with ASTM C738-94.</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Application Tips:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>3 brush coats recommended.\n<ul>\n<li>If you apply the glaze heavily, 2 coats will also work.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Best glazing brush to use: <a title=\"AMACO Fitch Fan Brush\" href=\"https://shop.amaco.com/fitch-fan-brush/\">AMACO Fitch Fan Brush.</a></li>\n<li>Underapplication will result in a dry glaze with no crystals.</li>\n<li>Overapplication will cause a rough appearance.\n<ul>\n<li>Can also lead to heavier flow.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span>Layers well over AMACO <a href=\"https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/c-celadon/\">Celadons</a>, other <a href=\"https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/\">Potter's Choice,</a> and <a href=\"https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/sm-satin-matte/\">Satin Matte</a> glazes. Glaze layering fired results may run if paired with a runny glaze. Apply receding coats when layering to help with runniness of final fired result. We recommend testing any layering combination before applying it to a full ceramic piece.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span>Fire to cone 6 when used alone or layered for results similar to AMACO imagery.</span></p>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Shake well before use. For best results, do not thin the glaze; apply 3 coats with a brush to Cone 04 bisque. (Let the glaze dry between coats.) Glaze fire to Cone 5-6. Due to variations in raw materials used during manufacturing, we recommend firing glazed test tiles before using each new batch of glaze.<span></span></div>",
